  <!-- /webdesign/samples/* is DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and so are /webdesign/thanks/
       and /webdesign/request-error/. Every one of them ships
       <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">, and listing a noindex
       page in a sitemap asks a crawler to index what the page tells it not to.

       The sample pages are demonstrations for businesses that are invented. If
       one were indexed, a search engine or an AI crawler could surface
       "Northfield Electric, Rockford IL" as a real company, which is the exact
       thing those pages are built not to do. For the same reason they are not
       described in llms.txt or llms-full.txt.

       They are NOT disallowed in robots.txt either, and that is on purpose: a
       Disallow stops a crawler fetching the page, so it never reads the noindex
       and a stale URL can sit in the index anyway. Permissive robots.txt plus
       a noindex tag is the combination that actually keeps them out. -->
